Ryan (Sales): Hey team — AtlasFinance POC streaming is failing on their iOS WebView during demo. Root cause looks like truncated JSON in the SSE stream, client throws 'Unexpected end of input'.

Sam (Eng): Can you paste the raw HTTP stream chunk logs? Is this SSE (event: message / data: ...) or raw chunked JSON?

Ryan (Sales): It's SSE from our hosted API at /v1/streams/generate. Leo captured the console: "JSON.parse error at byte 118: Unexpected end of input". He attached a partial dump:

Leo (Mobile): ```
event: message
data: {"id":"abc","choices":[{"delta":{"content":"Thank you for signing up. We will"},"index":0,"finish_reason":null}]

event: message
data: "continue the setup process by visiting https://..."}

```

Marta (DevEx): That looks like the second data event starts with a stray quote and a closing brace only — client-side concat is producing invalid JSON. iOS WebView's SSE parser sometimes hands chunks to JS before full event delim — can you confirm if the WebView is using the native EventSource polyfill or our SDK's stream parser?

Leo (Mobile): Using WebView + custom JS that listens to 'message' events, then does try { JSON.parse(e.data) } catch(e) { throw e }. Default EventSource on iOS is flaky in older WKWebView builds.

Sam (Eng): Two quick asks: 1) server-side raw bytes around the boundary (we need exact bytes, not pretty-printed), 2) the SDK version / browser agent string. Also, are you seeing any 429 bursts from our side? Rate limiter could be splitting payloads unpredictably when under backpressure.

Ryan (Sales): Attaching minimal repro steps:
- API: https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/generate
- Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>, Accept: text/event-stream
- Request body: {"model":"rw-large", "stream":true}
- Client: iOS WKWebView 14.3, JS EventSource polyfill v1.2.1

infra-bot: rate=200/60s burst=50; recent window shows occasional 429s from proxy at 2034567905 and 2034567951 (x-rw-retry-after: 1)

Sam (Eng): Ok infra note — proxy did return short 429 spikes. However that shouldn't corrupt chunk framing. Two hypotheses:
- Hyp A: our streaming proxy is buffering + flush-chunk boundaries incorrectly when a rate-limit/reset happens => results in a cut halfway through an event
- Hyp B: client polyfill mis-handles CRLF-only boundaries and concatenates adjacent 'data:' lines weirdly

Marta (DevEx): Short-term workaround for AtlasFinance: switch to our non-SSE streaming SDK (websocket / chunked-ndjson) or disable polyfill and use our official SDK's stream parser which buffers until a full JSON object. Also try setting `Accept: text/event-stream; charset=utf-8` to avoid any weird charset splitting.

Leo (Mobile): Can try SDK update in the demo. Do you have a small code snippet to buffer chunks until a newline then JSON.parse? current code parses every message event immediate.

Sam (Eng): Example pattern (do on client): ```
let buf = '';
es.addEventListener('message', e => {
  buf += e.data;
  try {
    const payload = JSON.parse(buf);
    buf = '';
    handle(payload);
  } catch (err) {
    // if invalid JSON, wait for next chunk
    if (err.message.includes('Unexpected end')) return;
    console.error('json parse failed', err);
    buf = '';
  }
});
```

Ryan (Sales): Would that hide genuine protocol errors though? Atlas needs deterministic behavior for demos.

Sam (Eng): It's a pragmatic buffer for broken event-splitting. We should still capture raw bytes and file a runtime bug. I'll triage with Eng Runtime — pinging @Sam (Eng) -> @runtime on Slack.

Marta (DevEx): Also, if you can toggle stream vs full resp in the POC: non-streaming (single JSON) will avoid this entirely. For demos it's often an acceptable fallback while we root cause.

Leo (Mobile): Trying SDK update now. ETA 20m to push a patched WebView demo that uses our SDK buffer.

Ryan (Sales): Atlas on standby — will update with their logs. Thanks all :thumbsup:

(10:02) Ryan (Sales): attached atlas_raw_stream.bin

Sam (Eng): Got the binary, running a byte-level reassembly now. Initial glance shows an event boundary cut at byte 1167 with no terminating CRLF before connection reset from their side. I'll follow up in this thread with findings.

(10:25) Sam (Eng): Follow-up — repro is confirmed: client-side event parsing + WebView handshake drop. Patch queued: runtime will ensure each SSE event is flushed atomically from the proxy when possible; also documenting client buffering pattern in the SDK guide. Will update with rollout ETA.

Ryan (Sales): Great — please keep me posted. Atlas wants a brief note for their security/compliance team that this is an interoperability bug (client polyfill + older WKWebView) and there's a recommended SDK workaround.

Marta (DevEx): I'll draft the note and the quickstart snippet. Putting this on the POC tracker.

infra-bot: deploy 2034568000 -> rollback not needed. monitored.

Leo (Mobile): Demo patched, confirmed parse success locally. Will run Atlas staging in 15.

Ryan (Sales): Thanks team! :rocket:
